0.7.16
- Added named, build-specific revision checkpoints for adapting plans across
  game updates, with the newest 20 revisions retained locally.
- Added keyboard and native gamepad revision browsers with save, restore, and
  delete actions. Restoring first keeps the replaced build as a new checkpoint.
- Kept revision history out of copied, imported, and shared builds so GBP1 codes
  remain compact and cannot contain nested backup histories.

0.7.15
- Enlarged the confirmation window and its message area so the character
  capture prompt wraps cleanly above the action buttons.

0.7.14
- Increased the keyboard Help page text to the normal game font for easier
  reading while retaining the three-page layout.
- Added confirmation prompts before keyboard or gamepad character capture.

0.7.13
- Replaced the unsupported owned-item checkmark character with ESO's native
  accept icon so completed gear no longer shows as a green rectangle.
- Used the same native completion icon in keyboard and gamepad checklists.

0.7.12
- Widened and rebalanced the Share window actions so Current Build Code and the
  localized Select and Import labels display in full.

0.7.11
- Split keyboard help into three pages so later sections no longer overflow the
  fixed text area or clip the Character heading and description.

0.7.10
- Widened the Preferred route label column and kept the route selector aligned
  with the editor's right edge so the label is no longer clipped.

0.7.9
- Separated the Champion Star point label from the equipment Champion Points
  label so the editor shows the intended short text without clipping.

0.7.8
- Kept the comparison header and result rows inside the panel's matching left
  and right insets so the header border no longer overruns the right edge.

0.7.7
- Moved the planner sections onto a dedicated navigation row below the build
  and setup controls so all seven sections remain readable without wrapping.
- Added room for the navigation row without reducing the planner workspace.

0.7.6
- Added one-click character snapshots that create a separate build from equipped
  gear, both action bars, attributes, race, Mundus Stone, curse, active class
  skill lines, and saved Champion Point allocations and slottables.
- Preserved exact equipped item links, traits, enchantments, quality, level, and
  two-handed weapon occupancy in the captured setup.
- Added Capture to the keyboard header and native gamepad build-management menu,
  with localized counts for the gear, skills, and Champion Stars copied.
- Kept capture transactional through the validated build importer so an invalid
  snapshot cannot leave a partial build behind.

0.7.5
- Added setup-specific Passive Skill, Skill Line, Unlock, and Other progression
  checklists with target ranks, notes, and completion tracking.
- Added passive-skill autocomplete from ESO's native skill data, rank-aware icons,
  and native keyboard and gamepad ability tooltips.
- Added keyboard and gamepad setup comparison that shows only changed defaults,
  gear and alternatives, skills, character choices, Champion Points, supplies,
  and checklist steps.
- Preserved progression checklists through migrations, setup and build copies,
  and GBP format-version 7 sharing while retaining imports from versions 1
  through 6.

0.7.4
- Added setup-specific food, drink, potion, poison, and other supply planning.
- Added saved-plan and inventory-backed item suggestions while still allowing
  free-text guide names and pasted item links.
- Added quantities, notes, item icons, and native tooltips to the keyboard
  Supplies view.
- Added native gamepad supply browsing, editing, removal, and item tooltips.
- Preserved consumable plans through migrations, setup and build copies, and
  GBP format-version 6 sharing while retaining imports from versions 1 through 5.

0.7.3
- Added Craft, Warfare, and Fitness Champion Point planning to each setup.
- Added Champion Star autocomplete from ESO's native Champion data, point caps,
  icons, and native keyboard and gamepad tooltips.
- Added passive-star allocations and four ordered slottable positions for each
  discipline without changing the player's live Champion bar.
- Added keyboard paging and a native gamepad allocation editor for larger plans.
- Preserved Champion plans through migrations, setup and build copies, and GBP
  format-version 5 sharing while retaining imports from versions 1 through 4.

0.7.2
- Added a Character view for setup-specific Health, Magicka, and Stamina
  allocations, with live totals and validation against ESO's 64-point limit.
- Added localized race and Mundus Stone selectors, a native Mundus icon, and
  None, Vampire, and Werewolf curse choices.
- Added three guide-friendly class skill-line fields for regular and subclassed
  builds.
- Added native gamepad character summaries and a controller character editor.
- Preserved character plans through migrations, setup and build copies, and GBP
  format-version 4 sharing while retaining imports from versions 1 through 3.

0.7.1
- Added Gear and Skills views without changing the existing equipment paper doll.
- Added front-bar and back-bar layouts with five active slots and one ultimate
  slot on each bar.
- Added active-skill and morph autocomplete from ESO's native skill data, with
  ultimate-only filtering for the sixth slot.
- Added planned skill icons, native keyboard and gamepad ability tooltips, and
  save and clear actions that never alter the player's equipped action bars.
- Used ESO's native ability-slot background for empty bar slots and previews.
- Added native gamepad skill-bar navigation and controller ability selection.
- Preserved both skill bars through setup and build copies, migrations, and GBP
  sharing while retaining support for version-1 and version-2 build codes.

0.7.0
- Added up to eight ordered fallback alternatives for each planned equipment slot.
- Added Primary, Alternative, and New Alternative choices to the keyboard and
  gamepad equipment editors.
- Added set-wide fallback application for replacing every matching piece of a
  primary set while preserving each slot's type, trait, enchantment, and level.
- Allowed owned fallback pieces to satisfy setup progress without increasing the
  number of planned slots or consuming one inventory item more than once.
- Made Shopping List choose one tradeable fallback when the primary requirement
  cannot be bought, rather than exporting every option as a separate purchase.
- Preserved alternatives through slot copies, moves, setup duplication, full-build
  sharing, and import. Existing GBP version-1 codes remain importable.

0.6.0
- Replaced the keyboard equipment list with an ESO-style paper-doll layout
  using the native player silhouette and empty-slot artwork.
- Arranged armor, jewelry, and both weapon bars like the Character window while
  preserving slot editing, tooltips, two-handed occupancy, and progress markers.
- Added checksummed GBP1 codes for backing up or sharing a complete build.
- Added transactional build import with fresh IDs, safe duplicate names, and no
  partial SavedVariables changes when a code is invalid.
- Preserved guide metadata, every setup, equipment requirements, item links,
  notes, setup defaults, preferred acquisition routes, and the selected setup.
- Added keyboard and native gamepad share and import workflows.
- Allowed Transmute and Unknown to be retained as preferred acquisition routes.

0.5.0
- Added LibSets as the complete set-name source, including crafted sets which do
  not appear in Item Set Collections.
- Added LibSets representative item links when a planned set has no collection
  piece, while keeping the existing trait, enchantment, quality, and level preview.
- Added LibSets armor-weight and crafted-set metadata to planning and acquisition.

0.4.0
- Added a native gamepad planner with controller navigation for equipment slots,
  builds, and setups.
- Added gamepad equipment editing with contextual type, trait, enchantment,
  quality, level, Champion Point, and note controls.
- Added native gamepad item tooltips, acquisition routes, progress totals, and
  copy, move, and clear actions.
- Added gamepad build and setup creation, renaming, duplication, reordering,
  deletion, and undo.
- Added gamepad Shopping List review and API v2 export, with a selectable SL2
  fallback code and add-on page link.
- Added native gamepad help and gamepad-aware slash command behavior.
- Reserved a setup-level data extension point for future alternate gear groups
  without changing the primary equipment-slot format.

0.3.0
- Replaced free-text enchantments with armor, jewelry, and weapon dropdowns.
- Added collection-piece resolution for matching armor, jewelry, and weapon slots.
- Added live representative item previews and native item tooltips on hover.
- Preserved older free-text enchantments as custom choices.
- Added a tooltip note when ESO's representative link uses a different default
  enchantment than the one planned.
- Replaced the preview text with the resolved item's icon.
- Added validated preview links for selected standard glyph enchantments.
- Made preview links honor per-slot or setup-default level and Champion Points.
- Labeled the Level and CP fields with their inherited setup defaults.
- Automatically selected and locked armor weight for fixed-weight collection sets.
- Kept all available weights selectable for monster sets and unrestricted manual sets.
- Added copy and move actions for compatible equipment slots, including safe
  handling for occupied off-hands and existing destination requirements.
- Added live acquisition classification for tradeable, crafted, reconstructable,
  bind-on-pickup, and unresolved equipment requirements.
- Added equipped, backpack, and bank matching with separate exact and adjustable
  results for trait, enchantment, and quality differences.
- Added readable acquisition routes with a saved preference when several routes
  are available.
- Added live setup totals for ready, adjustable, and missing equipment.
- Added Shopping List API v2 exports with a review of eligible, unavailable,
  and already-owned gear.
- Added optional separate glyph entries and upgrade-friendly quality matching.
- Added a selectable SL2 fallback code and a confirmed link to the Shopping
  List add-on page when the companion add-on is missing or outdated.
- Added in-game help for entering guide equipment, reading acquisition states,
  and exporting Shopping List entries.
- Added font scaling, high-contrast backdrops, standard control focus states,
  and optional text prefixes for status messages.
- Added resolver and native-tooltip coverage for representative overland,
  dungeon, trial, crafted, monster, mythic, arena, and perfected gear.
- Made Build Planner request ESO UI mode when opened, release only the cursor it
  requested, and restore that cursor after the game regains focus.

0.2.0
- Added the first keyboard and mouse planner window with fixed equipment slots.
- Added build and setup selectors, naming actions, deletion confirmation, and undo.
- Added set-name autocomplete from Item Set Collections and previously entered sets.
- Added contextual armor, weapon, trait, quality, level, enchantment, and note fields.
- Added a main-menu entry when LibMainMenu-2.0 is available, /buildplanner and
  /gbp commands, and a configurable keybinding.

0.1.0
- Added the initial account-wide build and setup data model.
- Added canonical armor, jewelry, and weapon slots with two-handed weapon handling.
- Added create, copy, reorder, delete, and undo operations for builds and setups.
- Added English, French, and Spanish foundation strings.
